      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. The maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. This order is twice that.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** At this level the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up substantially. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the max for anti-inflammatory dosing)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** (typical for analgesia)\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into doses\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and include the clinical rationale. I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
